# Vector-ownership director

You direct Team 3 only in the coordinator thread started from `handoff/cursor_bootstrap.md`. If this thread was not started that way, ignore this rule. Do not arm a watcher. Do not rotate.

They measure. You write the next prompt, check their section, and keep them on the vector-ownership gate. Do not append the trace yourself.

## Memory is the files, not the chat

On a wake (`AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_team3` or a reply in this coordinator thread):

1. Read the loop guard in `handoff/state.md`. If `status` is not `running`, stop and tell the user. Do not write a prompt.
2. Read `maps/vector_ownership/team3_next_prompt.txt`.
3. Read only the gate fields in `maps/vector_ownership/anomaly_vector_mutator_table.json`: `gate_status`, `gate_requirements`, `synchronization_contracts`.
4. Do not read `anomaly_begin_store_trace.txt` from the start. Read `handoff/team3_response.md` and only the last `=====` section. The response file is the wake. The new heading is the evidence. There is no `handoff/prompt.md`.

## When they reply

If the last heading is unchanged, stop. Do not write a prompt, do not commit, and do not run `handoff/rotate_threads.ps1`. Tell the user the loop paused.

If the section holds, replace `team3_next_prompt.txt` with the next question that moves synchronization, and update `handoff/state.md` in the same turn. If a sentence in the section is false, the next prompt corrects that sentence before the gate moves. Then run the rotator. If it exits nonzero, stop and tell the user.

Commit and push `team3_next_prompt.txt` only when a new heading holds and you replace the prompt. Do not commit a stop reply. Leave the trace, `handoff/team3_response.md`, and `handoff/state.md` unstaged.

## Prompt constraints, every time

Read-only copy project `v3d_files_uncomp_copy/V3D_SKIP`, program `/Vision3D.exe`. Do not save. Do not open the locked GUI project. If a lock file is present, report it and stop. Do not delete it. Close the headless session with `program_close` before finishing, and leave `program_list_open` at count 0. Do not open another module. Append under one new heading in `maps/vector_ownership/anomaly_begin_store_trace.txt`. Do not change the gate status.

Do not change `gate_status` until the synchronization half is proved or disproved. Do not arm `tools/team3_watch.ps1` or `handoff/watch_response.ps1` while the loop guard status is not `running`. One watcher only; the pid lock refuses a second copy.
